  DPV (NimbyDpv_Car) parts and storage rolled at spawn. Jeff's rulings, November 8, 2026, 01:30 to 01:40 Central (/interview after the draft of 01:25); D-5 of docs/design/dpv-feasibility.md (November 5, 2026: nominal 4, max 6, military sites only, per-part chance).
  DRAFT - not applied to the live server. The <type> below is ADDED to
  mpmissions/dayzOffline.nasdara/cfgspawnabletypes.xml (none exists there today). Everything not listed
  here is unchanged. Each <attachments> group rolls once at its chance and places at most one of its items,
  in the first free slot that item's inventorySlot[] shares with the car's attachments[] (NimbyDpv/config.cpp);
  item chances inside a group are weights that sum to 1.0, the vanilla convention (MP5K, VSS groups).

  Parts (Jeff, 01:37): the four road wheels at 1.00, so every spawned DPV stands on its wheels; the spare,
  battery, spark plug and two headlight bulbs at the OffroadHatchback values (0.40, 0.60, 0.60, 0.40, 0.40).
  Storage (Jeff, 01:38 and 01:39: "one roll per area" at the harsher odds): rail can 0.30, rail bag 0.40, rail
  tent 0.25, roof 0.30, first aid 0.40; about 1.6 pieces per DPV, about one DPV in seven bare. The roof twins
  share one group, so a bear and a crate never spawn together (the car's script refuses the second). Bag
  families are weighted equally and a family's colours split its weight; ImprovisedBag and FurImprovisedBag
  (crafted, nominal 0) and SlingBag (no class in the 1.30 types.xml) are left out. The 21 AmmoBox_* classes
  are ammunition, not the AmmoBox container, and are not listed.
-->
